& [ReconciledRuntimeInvariantSet: IR4] is the reconciled invariant set for IR4 runtime planning
  + [invariant] is SOP files and accepted proof packs remain source authority
  + [invariant] is LangGraph graph state is execution state only
  + [invariant] is LangGraph checkpoint state is execution state only
  + [invariant] is graph nodes may invoke only accepted operator contracts or accepted operator harness functions inside declared scope
  + [invariant] is every success, blocked, stale, fault, and interrupt path must preserve or emit operator_trace evidence
  + [invariant] is runtime outputs consumed by future surfaces must carry non-authority status unless accepted by a completion review
  + [invariant] is SOP-first interrupt pauses mutation until accepted resume evidence exists
  + [invariant] is completion_review_delta_gate remains the only accepted next-gate control contract
  + [invariant] is checkpoint authority confusion is a fault, not a source of truth

  = must: preserve these invariants through IR4-S02 through IR4-S06
  = must: route invariant contradictions through completion review and rebake rather than silent edits

& [OperatorHarnessRuntimeHandoff: IR4] is the handoff from IR3 operator harness proof into IR4 graph planning
  + [handoff_source] is IR3OperatorHarnessImplementationProofPackV1
  + [operator_contract_validation] is available through accepted IR3 contracts.py
  + [trace_event_model] is available through accepted IR3 traces.py
  + [runner_classification] is available through accepted IR3 runner.py after repair
  + [fixture_path_policy] is available through accepted IR3 fixture_runner.py after repair
  + [handoff_limit] is fixture-scale proof only; no live dispatch, job control, process control, GPU control, network control, credential access, operations control, or live machine control

  = must: make future graph implementation call operator-harness functions only through bounded in-process fixture/runtime contracts
  = must: refuse any graph node that tries to use operator harness proof as permission for live work dispatch

& [RuntimeCheckpointAndTraceAuthorityBoundary: IR4] is the checkpoint and trace authority boundary
  + [checkpoint_role] is generated execution continuation state
  + [checkpoint_not_role] is signed authority, accepted decision, completion review, coordination claim acceptance, or source specification
  + [operator_trace_role] is generated projection evidence with lineage to accepted inputs
  + [operator_trace_not_role] is source authority by itself
  + [checkpoint_stale_trigger] is changed source authority, changed proof pack, changed graph contract, changed operator contract, changed trace schema, changed fixture expectation, changed resume condition, or checkpoint policy change
  + [trace_stale_trigger] is changed source authority, changed operator contract, changed input record, changed graph node contract, changed trace schema, or generated output policy change

  = must: reject checkpoint resume when freshness cannot be proven
  = must: require SOP-first interrupt or stale terminal state when checkpoint authority confusion is detected

& [ForbiddenRuntimeMutationList: IR4] is the forbidden mutation set for IR4 runtime planning
  + [forbidden_mutation] is editing accepted FSC3 or IR3 proof outputs to make runtime proof easier
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating graph state as authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating checkpoint state as authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating generated traces or reports as authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing executable LangGraph nodes
  + [forbidden_mutation] is installing LangGraph or other dependencies
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing checkpoint persistence
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing surface adapters
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating runtime fixtures before fixture slices open
  + [forbidden_mutation] is authorizing operations control or live machine control

  = must: fail IR4-S01 review if any forbidden mutation appears in the output

& [DownstreamStaleTriggerList: IR4] is the stale trigger set for downstream IR4 work
  + [stale_trigger] is FSC3 runtime graph proof pack hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR3 operator harness implementation proof pack hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR3 implementation completion review changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR4 final slice surface changes
  + [stale_trigger] is runtime invariant contradiction
  + [stale_trigger] is checkpoint authority confusion
  + [stale_trigger] is hidden graph write
  + [stale_trigger] is missing operator_trace on graph path output
  + [stale_trigger] is false-ready surface or checkpoint state

  = must: mark affected downstream slices stale when any listed trigger fires
  = must: route stale-trigger repair through completion review rather than silent edits

